       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg per day. Higher doses mostly add peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, with little extra blood pressure benefit.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the standard maximum dose.\n2. **A different plan.** If 10 mg isn't enough, I can enter a second agent instead, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-like diuretic. You'd need to tell me the drug and dose.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written.** If you have a specific reason for the above-maximum dose, confirm that and I'll enter it. I'll add a note that the dose is intentional."
